implementationPlan.description:
Render the section in moe-vscode/src/panels/TaskDetailPanel.ts.
- Add `private renderDelivery(task: Task): string` and call it in getWebviewContent directly after `<div id="blockerSection">...</div>`. That is the order JetBrains' TaskDetailDialog uses: blocker, then delivery, then the editable fields.
- It returns '' when deliveryRows(task.delivery) is empty. Otherwise it returns exactly this markup, each row on one line, which step 1's test matches:
  - open: `<div class="delivery-section" id="deliverySection"><div class="section-title">${escapeHtml(DELIVERY_LABELS[DELIVERY_TITLE_KEY])}</div>`;
  - per row: `<div class="delivery-row[ delivery-pass| delivery-fail]"><div class="field-label">${escapeHtml(label)}</div><div class="delivery-value" title="${escapeHtml(row.fullValue)}">${escapeHtml(row.value)}</div></div>`, where label = DELIVERY_LABELS[row.labelKey] ?? row.labelKey;
  - close: `</div>`.
- Every daemon-supplied string is runner-reported text and goes through the existing escapeHtml. Never interpolate one raw.
- Add CSS next to .blocker-text:
  - `.delivery-section { margin-bottom: 12px; }`;
  - `.delivery-value { font-size: 12px; font-family: var(--vscode-editor-font-family); white-space: pre-wrap; word-wrap: break-word; }`;
  - `.delivery-pass .delivery-value { color: var(--vscode-testing-iconPassed); }`;
  - `.delivery-fail .delivery-value { color: var(--vscode-testing-iconFailed); }`.
- The section is read only: no action, no copy button, no client call (the strict client stubs in three peer tests would throw).
- Leave live refresh through media/taskDetail.js out of scope. VSC-11 edits that file, and the architect noted the gap on the epic-final row VSC-18. Leave media/taskDetail.js unchanged.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff, the only review step.
- Would the corpus test still pass if deliveryRows:
  - used `treeSha ?? shortSha` (D04 must fail);
  - cut a non-SHA target (D15);
  - inferred the policy verdict from the last run (D13, D14);
  - whitelisted an unknown outcome as passed (D10);
  - returned undefined instead of null outcomes (the JSON round trip must make that fail);
  - or emitted rows in JSON member order (D16)?
- Would the HTML test fail if escapeHtml were dropped from the value or from the title attribute? Does any daemon string reach the HTML without escapeHtml?
- Malformed input (numbers, arrays, null members, a string exitCode) must never throw.
- No value import was added to TaskDetailPanel.ts, and no new client member is touched.
- Confirm with `git status --porcelain` that the task touched only moe-vscode/src/types/moe.ts, moe-vscode/src/panels/TaskDetailPanel.ts and moe-vscode/tests/delivery-corpus.test.cjs.
- Confirm `git diff --exit-code HEAD -- moe-jetbrains/src/test/resources/client-delivery.json moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties` exits 0 (DoD 4; after landing, QA checks `git diff --exit-code <landing>^ <landing> -- moe-jetbrains`).
- Peers own every other dirty path: never revert, stage or commit them.
- Report the three files in complete_step.modifiedFiles.
